Done. Here's what I implemented:

Lua support — 4 regex patterns covering:
• function name() — top-level global functions
• local function name() — file-scoped functions
• function M.name() / function M:name() — module methods (dot and colon notation)
• M.name = function() — assigned module functions
• Comment lines (`-- ...) naturally skipped since they don't match ^function` etc.

Zig support — 4 regex patterns covering:
• pub fn name() / fn name() — public and private functions
• `pub const Name = struct / const Name = struct — struct definitions (including extern`/packed variants)
• pub const Name = enum — enum definitions
• pub const Name = union — union definitions
• Test blocks (`test "name"`) naturally skipped — no pattern matches them
• New StartsWithPub visibility rule for Zig's pub convention

Tests — 11 new tests covering all symbol types, comment skipping, test skipping, plus a regression test confirming Rust and Python extraction still works.
